==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|schilt}}, from {{inh|de|goh|scilt}}, {{m|goh|scild}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*skelduz||shield}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*(s)keyt-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*(s)keyd-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*keyt-||shield, cover}}. Compare {{cog|nl|schild}}, {{cog|en|shield}}, {{cog|da|skjold}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ʃɪlt/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Schild.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}
* {{homophones|schilt|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m|g2=n|Schilds|gen2=Schildes|Schilde}}

# [[shield]], [[buckler]]

====Usage notes====
In official use ([[Standard German]]), the word ''Schild'' in this sense is exclusively masculine. However, in large parts of Germany, namely Northern and Central Germany, the word is also used in the neuter variant (plural ''Schilder'') with no difference made between ''shield'' and ''sign''. <ref>[http://www.wienerzeitung.at/meinungen/glossen/389738_Der-Schild-oder-das-Schild.html Der Schild oder das Schild?], Wiener Zeitung Online</ref>

